     1,
     "Hi, I am new to Bayesian inference and a bit lost trying to find the best way to model the data for one of my studies. <div><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:15px;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit;color:rgb(12,13,14)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:15px;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">I am trying to predict distance cycled based on population density, recreational area density, infrastructure density, road intersection density, and average gradient (hilliness). The response variable, distance cycled (km cycled per year), is continuous and strongly skewed to the right (see histogram below). Therefore, I was considering using a Gamma regression model.</span></div><div><font color=\"#0c0d0e\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><br></span></font><div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding-top:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:13px;vertical-align:top;box-sizing:inherit;width:auto;min-width:0px;color:rgb(12,13,14)\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;width:654.219px\"><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://i.stack.imgur.com/WND1T.png\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;text-decoration-line:underline;box-sizing:inherit\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://i.stack.imgur.com/WND1T.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792435943652000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Ef8gd8fFtgqKFfkNdrlmx\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/66KLD_w0EI5PYjvrLtuCCH5P6G8bfM-qvk8UxxrVWRr8huZaxlzGRQ6PVt8TDq5n0jQHQIOY=s0-d-e1-ft#https://i.stack.imgur.com/WND1T.png\" alt=\"enter image description here\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border-width:0px;border-style:initial;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;vertical-align:bottom;box-sizing:inherit;max-width:100%\"></a></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\">However, the data is areal (aggregated for small areas within a region) and <span style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\">according to a Moran&#39;s I test there is spatial autocorrelation in my model.</span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\"> So I also need to account for spatial autocorrelation.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\">I have looked at the Besag-York-Mollié (BYM) model (popular in disease mapping) included in the R-INLA R package. Still, I am not sure whether it would be suitable for my continuous outcome distance cycled.</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\">I would appreciate some help with this from those who have experience modeling areal data with a continuous dependent variable. Thank you!</p></div></div></div></div>"
